cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use MilAMin, please cite it as below, together with the 2008 MILAMIN paper.
type: software
title: "MilAMin: MILAMIN in the browser"
abstract: >-
  The MILAMIN finite element pipeline in the browser: Stokes flow on
  unstructured triangular meshes with 7-node Crouzeix-Raviart elements,
  Triangle meshing, supernodal Cholesky factorization and Powell-Hestenes
  pressure iterations, in TypeScript and WebAssembly. A million unknowns a
  minute on a phone, verified against analytical solutions. Playground,
  benchmark, convergence lab and Folder for folding and boudinage.
authors:
